# Hydration-safe first paint

INVARIANT: The first client render of any component must be byte-identical to the
server HTML. Derived entirely from props. Nothing else.

BANNED in render paths:
- localStorage / sessionStorage / document.cookie reads → useState(serverProp),
  read external state in useEffect, or move it to a cookie the server layout reads
- matchMedia / useReducedMotion / navigator.* / typeof window branches in render
- Math.random(), Date.now() in initial render
- toLocaleString()/toLocaleDateString() → use ~/lib/toronto-time
  (`Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-CA', { timeZone: 'America/Toronto' })`)
- Random inline styles/colors → derive deterministically (charCode sums over an id)

WHEN A HYDRATION ERROR APPEARS:
1. QUOTE THE DIFF (the -/+ lines) before proposing any fix. If you cannot see
   the diff, say so and ask for it. Never guess a cause.
2. Classify first:
   - Extension fingerprints (data-gr-ext-installed, data-new-gr-c-s-*,
     bis_skin_checked, bis_register, __processed_*) → browser extension, NOT
     app code. Do not change code. Tell me to verify in incognito.
   - Anything else → name the exact file and line; fix by making first paint
     deterministic (server prop + useEffect, or cookie read server-side).
3. NEVER: suppressHydrationWarning on a parent to hide an undiagnosed mismatch,
   add mounted-gates as a first resort, or refactor a component without a diff.
   suppressHydrationWarning is allowed only per-element after diagnosis
   (theme `<html>`, `<body>` for extensions, specific inputs Grammarly touches).
4. Before claiming fixed, state: which route, hard reload with console open,
   and which server props/cookies feed the first paint.
